WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:04.270
A good movie title should be memorable, but
they don't always have to make sense.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:08.840
On occasion, filmmakers end up with titles
that are wildly—and sometimes hilariously—inaccurate.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:14.580
Here are some movie titles that lied straight
to your face.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.340
The Lone Ranger

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.200
In no iteration of The Lone Ranger is the
heroic cowboy actually lonesome; his sidekick,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.200
Tonto, is always by his side.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.090
As a character, Tonto is almost as famous
as the Lone Ranger—in fact, in the 2013

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:32.410
movie adaptation, the guy who played Tonto,
Johnny Depp, even earned top billing over

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.260
the guy playing the Lone Ranger, Armie Hammer.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.260
Fargo

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.550
The only scene in this Coen Brothers classic
that's actually set in Fargo, North Dakota,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.190
is the one when Jerry meets with the two hitmen
to set up the kidnapping of his wife.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.589
The rest of the movie takes place in Minnesota,
specifically in Brainerd.

00:00:52.589 --> 00:00:53.640
"Brainerd?"

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.739
"Yeah, yeah.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:00:57.800
Home of Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox."

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.610
Sure, you could argue that calling the movie
"Brainerd" wouldn't be as exciting, and the

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.160
meeting in Fargo spirals out into all kinds
of craziness, but it's still the equivalent

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.820
of Gotham taking place in Metropolis.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.190
You'd think that two seasons of the awesome
Fargo TV series would correct the location

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.580
a bit, right?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.580
Wrong!

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:17.580
"Double whoops."

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.030
Most of the series takes place in other towns
throughout Minnesota, North Dakota, and South

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:26.100
Dakota, with Fargo visited only a few times
throughout the show.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.090
"You do know you're in North Dakota, right?

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.940
Friday the 13th: The Final Chapter

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:35.220
Yes, the fourth movie in the Friday the 13th
franchise is indeed the final installment

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.650
in the saga of drowning victim-turned hockey
mask-wearing mass murderer Jason Voorhees.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:46.720
"But now, Jason's reign of terror is over."

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:51.710
We all thought Friday the 13th Part IV was
going to be "The Final Chapter" when it came

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:56.580
to Jason, but little did horror fans know
that there'd still be Friday the 13th Part

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.600
V: A New Beginning, Friday the 13th Part VI:
Jason Lives, Friday the 13th Part VII: The

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:09.119
New Blood, Friday the 13th Part VIII: Jason
Takes Manhattan, Jason Goes to Hell: The Final

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:15.680
Friday, Jason X—the one where he goes to
outer space, the 2003 crossover Freddy Vs.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.750
Jason, and the 2009 Friday the 13th reboot.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.530
Batman Forever

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:23.060
Not quite forever.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:27.730
The third big-screen Batman movie obviously
couldn't have an infinite running time, though

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.319
this thing certainly seems like it never ends.

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:31.319
"Exactly."

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:36.780
But it did well enough at the box office to
generate a sequel, Batman &amp; Robin.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:41.019
That one was so poorly received that it prevented
the Batman franchise from going on forever.

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:42.749
"What killed the dinosaurs?

00:02:42.749 --> 00:02:45.269
The ice age!"

00:02:45.269 --> 00:02:50.030
Another Batman movie wouldn't be made until
almost a decade later, with Christopher Nolan's

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:53.180
franchise reboot Batman Begins.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:54.749
The Karate Kid

00:02:54.749 --> 00:03:00.330
Everything about the 1984 original The Karate
Kid is unassailable, including its title,

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.999
although 23-year-old Ralph Macchio stretched
the definition of "kid.”

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:08.560
But the 2010 remake, starring Jaden Smith,
isn't about karate at all.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.370
In this version, Jackie Chan teaches his young
charge kung fu, not karate.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:19.180
Considering Kung Fu comes from China and Karate
comes from Japan, having a movie where Chinese

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:24.820
action star Jackie Chan teaches Kung Fu to
a boy living in China and calling it "The

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:28.019
Karate Kid" is a downright lie.

00:03:28.019 --> 00:03:29.719
Mission: Impossible

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:34.669
All of Tom Cruise’s top secret spy missions
as Ethan Hunt turn out to be possible after

00:03:34.669 --> 00:03:36.440
all, even if they are pretty difficult.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.819
Viewers can tell Hunt's missions aren't impossible
thanks to the existence of multiple sequels—if

00:03:41.819 --> 00:03:45.889
any of them really were impossible, he and
his whole team would be dead.

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:47.019
"Whoo!

00:03:47.019 --> 00:03:50.040
That was not easy, but I did it."

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.040
Jurassic Park

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.120
Yeah, it takes place at Jurassic Park.

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.079
"Welcome to Jurassic Park!"

00:03:58.079 --> 00:04:02.549
But it should really be named Cretaceous Park,
because nearly all of the dinosaurs in Jurassic

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:05.079
Park actually date to the Cretaceous period.

00:04:05.079 --> 00:04:09.260
"Alan this form of species has been extinct
since the Cretaceous period."

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:14.060
The Jurassic era came before the Cretaceous—by
about 80 million years.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.200
Now if only they could explain that to the
dinosaurs…

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.150
Thanks for watching!

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.780
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.150
And leave us a comment to let us know which
inaccurate movie titles we missed…

